    "narrative": "The primary objective for LawDog today is maximizing output against mid-tier starting pitching, and our highest-upside play is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (86.57). Facing Young, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a 13% SP skill bump, positioning him as an elite anchor for the daily total. He is closely followed by **Lawrence Butler** (74.31) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52). **Dylan Beavers** is particularly fascinating today; while the matchup against Bibee carries some risk, the combination of a high-park-factor environment and the opposing catcher\u2019s slow delivery (+4% SB adjustment) makes him a vital play in our pursuit of stolen bases, which remains our scarcest category. **Bryce Harper** (73.06) also remains a core engine for the lineup, with a strong xwOBA of .392 anchoring his sustained efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Braden Montgomery** (52.95) out of the starting nine. While his 19% SP skill bump against Chandler was compelling, he simply failed to clear the threshold established by **Justin Crawford** (59.21) and **Masyn Winn** (51.94), who maintain better positional utility and volume today. We are also monitoring **Cal Raleigh** (56.63) closely; while he is a staple, his 5% park penalty and dynamic platoon disadvantage against Quantrill make him the most vulnerable starter in our current configuration. We have successfully bypassed the \"Below Floor\" trap set by the matchup against Skubal, keeping **JJ Bleday** (46.47) and **Kyle Karros** (38.21) benched to preserve our game caps for more favorable conditions, especially given that **Kyle Karros** fell well below our internal 40.0 efficiency requirement.",
